{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK4ZULS5AgVfnZ4q3rsK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`FilePathField`'s `path` can now be a callable. The `model_fields` and FilePathField form tests pass: 270 tests ran, 48 skipped.\n\n**The fix:** a one-line change in `FilePathField.formfield()` in `django/db/models/fields/__init__.py`. When the form field is built, if `path` is a callable, Django calls it and uses the result as the directory. A plain string path works the same as before.\n\n**Why it fixes the migrations problem:** migrations store whatever you pass as `path`. If you pass a function, `makemigrations` records a reference to the function instead of the path resolved on your machine. Each machine then works out the directory at runtime. The function must be defined at module level so migrations can serialize a reference to it:\n\n```python\ndef local_files_path():\n    return os.path.join(settings.LOCAL_FILE_DIR, 'example_dir')\n\nclass LocalFiles(models.Model):\n    file = models.FilePathField(path=local_files_path)\n```\n\nI didn't update the docs (`docs/ref/models/fields.txt`) or add a release note, since you asked for the smallest fix."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":213,"cache_read_input_tokens":19383,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":213},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0f45528-0fa1-4022-9fa8-19e7e5922819","uuid":"7bf898e7-ae3d-4246-98f8-fbd9ee6c3057","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:21:47.831Z","request_id":"req_011ChK4ZUBzNFwk3ZrjeYvUv"}
